1
00:00:00,876 --> 00:00:02,377
Hey.

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:04,003
What's the matter?

3
00:00:04,045 --> 00:00:06,799
Somebody on the subway
licked my neck-- licked my neck!

4
00:00:06,841 --> 00:00:09,217
Oh! Willy's still alive.

5
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,428
What are you guys
doing?

6
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:14,473
My mom called. They're going to
run our engagement announcement

7
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:16,141
in the local paper,
so I'm looking

8
00:00:16,183 --> 00:00:17,392
for a good
picture of us.

9
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,144
Ooh, I'm afraid
that does not exist.

10
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:21,814
That's not true.
There are great pictures of us.

11
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:23,524
No, there are great
pictures of you

12
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:25,818
standing next to a guy
who's going like this.

13
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,822
Oh, my God! That's the creep
that you're with

14
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:31,198
at the Statue of Liberty!

15
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:33,868
I don't know what it is.

16
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:35,870
I just can't take
a good picture.

17
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:37,872
Hmm, here's a great one.

18
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:39,832
Yeah. I'm not in that.

19
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:42,501
I know, but look at me, all tan.

20
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:44,628
Hey, why don't you guys
go get portraits done

21
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,087
by a professional photographer?

22
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:47,589
That's a great idea!

23
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,048
I bet they have one
of those wind machines--

24
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,091
you know, like...

25
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,092
( imitating wind )

26
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,178
Yeah, that's great.

27
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,472
Next to that,
Chandler won't look so stupid.

28
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:58,726
So, Chandler,
what do you say?

29
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,520
All right, but I should
warn you: I'm not going.

30
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:02,563
I'm going.

31
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:13,532
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

32
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,576
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

33
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,704
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

34
00:01:18,746 --> 00:01:23,458
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

35
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,627
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

36
00:01:25,669 --> 00:01:29,048
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

37
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:32,384
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

38
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:35,888
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

39
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:43,771
Dude, that reverse
lay-up...

40
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:45,689
Oh! And how about
those three-pointers?

41
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:46,899
Amazing!

42
00:01:46,941 --> 00:01:48,191
And those guys
were this close

43
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,902
to letting us play
this time, too.

44
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:58,201
Hey, look, look--
Phoebe's talking to, uh,
"cute coffeehouse guy."

45
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:00,287
Oh, you guys call him
"Cute Coffeehouse Guy"?

46
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:03,331
We call him
"Hums While He Pees."

47
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:07,753
Yes, and we call Ross
"Lingers in the Bathroom."

48
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:09,128
Hey, you guys?

49
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,423
"Hums While He Pees"
just asked me out.

50
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,551
Wait, I thought
that guy was married.

51
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,511
He is,
but he's getting divorced.

52
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:18,055
Ross, maybe you know him.

53
00:02:19,932 --> 00:02:22,893
It's not a club.

54
00:02:22,935 --> 00:02:24,812
Phoebe, if this guy's
going through a divorce

55
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,981
is it such a good idea
to start going out with him?

56
00:02:27,022 --> 00:02:29,066
Hey, divorced men
are not bad men.

57
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:31,735
They have that on the
napkins at the club.

58
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,738
Oh, I got to get
back to work.

59
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,991
You don't have to be back
for a half hour.

60
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:38,241
Yeah, but my assistant Tag

61
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:39,994
does sit-ups in the office
during lunch.

62
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,328
( sighing )

63
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:44,123
Oh, I could just
spread him on a cracker.

64
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:49,419
Rach, if you have
a crush on this guy,
why would you hire him?

65
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:51,212
I mean, you know can't
date him, right?

66
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:52,840
Oh, no, I know that,
I know that...

67
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:54,382
although we made
a joke, though

68
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:56,093
that we spend
so much time together

69
00:02:56,135 --> 00:02:57,719
he should call me
his work wife.

70
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,763
Soon he'll be able to call you

71
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:02,141
"That Lady He Knew
That Got Fired."

72
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:03,809
I'm not going to get fired

73
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:06,020
because I'm not going
to act on it.

74
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:08,438
So, then, you wouldn't mind
if he was dating someone else?

75
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,648
Why? Is he?

76
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:10,983
He is, isn't he?

77
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:13,318
He's dating that slut
in marketing.

78
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:17,114
Maybe I should open
a divorced men's club.

79
00:03:17,156 --> 00:03:19,783
Dude, that's so sad.

80
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:22,243
I can put a basketball court
in the back.

81
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:23,370
( laughing )

82
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:24,955
Could I play?

83
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:31,628
Oh.

84
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,630
No sit-ups today, Tag?

85
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,049
I just did them.

86
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:37,467
Oh... Well, drop and give me
ten more.

87
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:39,302
What?

88
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:41,429
I-I had a drink with lunch.

89
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,515
Did those, um...

90
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:45,100
Did those cost reports
come in?

91
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:47,102
Yeah. I filled them out
last night.

92
00:03:47,144 --> 00:03:49,146
Oh, great. Could you make me
four copies of those?

93
00:03:49,188 --> 00:03:50,147
Sure.

94
00:03:50,189 --> 00:03:51,773
Great. Thank you.

95
00:03:58,113 --> 00:03:59,781
Mmm...

96
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:03,744
Huh.

97
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:08,790
Oh...

98
00:04:10,876 --> 00:04:12,544
Hey, Rachel.

99
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:14,838
( gasping ):
Oh, hi. Hi, Melissa, what's up?

100
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,882
I'm just, uh, I'm just
about to, uh...

101
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:19,093
go out to the store

102
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:21,136
and get some stuff
to put in my backpack--

103
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:23,346
you know, like,
dried fruit
and granola

104
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,598
and stuff like that.

105
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:25,599
Uh, what's up?

106
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,059
Is Tag here?

107
00:04:27,101 --> 00:04:28,643
No. Why?

108
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:30,979
Oh, well, I was going
to talk to him about doing

109
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,647
something tonight,
mm-hmm.

110
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:35,525
You got a little crush
on Tag there, do ya?

111
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,986
Well, we've been flirting
back and forth

112
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:41,240
but I was hoping tonight
it would turn into something

113
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:42,783
a little more than that.

114
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:45,035
Oh, okay. Whoa, whoa,
easy there, Melissa.

115
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:48,247
This ain't a
locker room, okay?

116
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:51,416
But, you know,
I remember him saying

117
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:54,335
that-that he had plans tonight.

118
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,045
Oh, no.

119
00:04:55,087 --> 00:04:57,256
Oh, yeah.

120
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:59,007
All right, back to work.

121
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:02,761
Hey, isn't that
Tag's backpack?

122
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:05,680
Yeah. Melissa, you know,
I don't want to be known

123
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:09,184
as the, uh, office bitch,
but I will call your supervisor.

124
00:05:15,107 --> 00:05:16,066
Great.

125
00:05:16,108 --> 00:05:17,692
That's great, Monica.

126
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:18,819
Great.

127
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,487
Now, Chandler,
you want to give us

128
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,655
a smile?

129
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:23,240
Okay.

130
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:29,079
I'm sorry, is the seat
uncomfortable?

131
00:05:29,121 --> 00:05:30,580
No. I am.

132
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:33,292
Chandler, sweetie, I know
you can do this, okay?

133
00:05:33,332 --> 00:05:34,876
You have a beautiful smile.

134
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:35,585
I do?

135
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:36,377
Yeah!

136
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:40,757
All right, maybe you
don't have to smile.

137
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:42,134
Let's try something else.

138
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:44,343
Let's try, um...
try looking sexy.

139
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,512
Okay.

140
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,228
Or not.

141
00:05:58,692 --> 00:06:01,236
Hi, Joey! What are
you doing here?

142
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:03,030
Uh, well, I got an audition
down the street

143
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,240
and I spilled sauce all over
the front of my shirt.

144
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:07,784
You got an extra one?

145
00:06:07,826 --> 00:06:09,161
Yeah, sure.

146
00:06:09,203 --> 00:06:11,579
Uh...

147
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:12,706
Here.

148
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,499
Great.

149
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:18,837
You got anything that's
not Ralph Lauren?

150
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:22,174
Yeah, I-I don't
think so, Joe.

151
00:06:22,216 --> 00:06:25,802
All right, I guess
this'll be fine.

152
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:28,096
Hey, listen, what are you
doing tonight?

153
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:29,848
Nothing. Why?

154
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:32,767
How would you feel about taking
out my assistant, Tag? I'll pay.

155
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:36,271
Rach, I gotta say,
it's gonna take a lot of money

156
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:39,107
for me to go out on a date
with a dude.

157
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:42,569
I'm not asking you to go out
on a date with him.

158
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:45,739
Really? 'Cause I could kind of
use the money.

159
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,448
Joey, just-just,
he's new in town

160
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:49,784
and I know he doesn't
have any guy friends.

161
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:52,329
Just take him to, like,
a ballgame or something.

162
00:06:52,371 --> 00:06:53,747
I'd really appreciate it.

163
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,456
Yeah, okay, sure,
no problem.

164
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,457
Thank you.

165
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,834
Ooh! Hey, doughnuts.

166
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:59,336
Yeah.

167
00:06:59,378 --> 00:07:01,004
Okay.

168
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,136
I know.

169
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:12,182
Let's try a look of
far-off wonderment, okay?

170
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:14,226
We'll gaze into our future

171
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:16,519
and we'll think
about our marriage

172
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,479
and the days to come.

173
00:07:23,277 --> 00:07:26,487
Chandler, what is the matter
with your face?!

174
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,864
This picture is
supposed to say

175
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:29,824
"Geller and Bing
to be married"

176
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,869
not "Local woman
saves drowning moron."

177
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,247
( chuckling )

178
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:36,539
Hey, don't laugh
at him.

179
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,208
He's my drowning moron.

180
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,127
Aw...

181
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:41,878
That's it! That's it!
Take it, take it.

182
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:49,344
I like this one.

183
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:50,762
It seems to say

184
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:53,556
"I love you, and that's
why I have to kill you.'

185
00:07:55,392 --> 00:07:57,477
They can't all be bad.

186
00:07:57,518 --> 00:08:00,688
Find the one where you
make your bedroom eyes.

187
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,316
Oh, there it is.

188
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:05,484
Oh, my God, those are
my bedroom eyes?

189
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:08,863
Why did you ever
sleep with me?

190
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:11,908
Do you really want to
pull at that thread?

191
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:18,206
( laughing ):
I'm having
a really good time.

192
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:19,582
Me, too.

193
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,376
Sorry that guy on the subway
licked your neck.

194
00:08:21,418 --> 00:08:24,171
Oh, no, that's okay.

195
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:25,546
He's a friend.

196
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,382
Hey, uh, I don't mean
to be presumptuous

197
00:08:27,424 --> 00:08:28,758
but I have
these two tickets

198
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,885
to the Ballroom Dancing
Finals tomorrow night

199
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:31,845
if you want to go.

200
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,263
Yeah.

201
00:08:33,305 --> 00:08:35,515
I... well, you know,
I missed the semifinals

202
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:38,143
so I think I would
just be lost.

203
00:08:38,185 --> 00:08:39,978
Look, I know that
it's really lame

204
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,397
but I got these tickets
from my boss, and...

205
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:45,275
Oh, no, no, no.
My God...

206
00:08:45,317 --> 00:08:48,028
Okay, don't freak out. I'll go.

207
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:49,112
My ex-wife Whitney
is out there.

208
00:08:49,154 --> 00:08:51,072
I cannot deal with her
right now.

209
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:52,991
That woman is crazy.

210
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,285
Okay, I know. Hold on.

211
00:08:55,327 --> 00:08:56,577
Hey, Ross?

212
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,121
Yeah?

213
00:08:58,163 --> 00:09:00,999
Um, that's Whitney,
Kyle's ex-wife, out there.

214
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:03,668
Now, do you think you could,
you know, divert her

215
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:04,919
so we could slip out?

216
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:06,129
What?! No.

217
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:08,048
Well, okay.

218
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:12,344
But I have two tickets
to the Ballroom Dance Finals...

219
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:14,804
Look, I don't think so, Pheebs.

220
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:19,226
( sighing ):
All right, I'll do it.

221
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,019
Oh.

222
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:23,271
But just because
you're a friend.

223
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:24,314
Okay.

224
00:09:35,574 --> 00:09:37,452
D-ohh!

225
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:39,954
Hi, Ginger.

226
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:41,789
All right, I want my key back.

227
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:42,707
I don't have it.

228
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:43,666
It's right there.

229
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,293
( groaning )

230
00:09:45,335 --> 00:09:47,045
Okay, Sherlock.

231
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:50,048
All right, I'm sorry,
but you'd better go, Pheebs.

232
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:52,259
All right. I just wanted
to say thank you, though

233
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,385
for diverting Kyle's ex.

234
00:09:53,427 --> 00:09:54,469
Oh, yeah, no, you're welcome.

235
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:55,512
We'll talk about it later.

236
00:09:55,554 --> 00:09:56,555
Okay.

237
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,307
Hi, Whitney.

238
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:01,601
Hi, Ross.

239
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:02,810
You... ready for breakfast?

240
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:04,312
Yep... oops.

241
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,065
Kyle's ex-wife?

242
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:09,359
You were supposed to divert her,
not date her.

243
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:12,571
Hi. I'm sorry.

244
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,989
Can you give me a second
while I talk to this woman

245
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:17,451
uh, who, by the way,
did not spend the night?

246
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,411
Sure.

247
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:21,246
Okay.

248
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:26,667
I did divert her, and we ended
up having a great time, okay?

249
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,420
Watching ballroom dancing?

250
00:10:28,462 --> 00:10:31,798
Yes. That's where we realized
we were both supercool people.

251
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,301
Well, look, okay, Ross.

252
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:37,095
Kyle just told me some
really bad stuff about her.

253
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,138
Like, like what?

254
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:40,390
Like she's
really mean

255
00:10:40,432 --> 00:10:42,350
and she's overly critical,
and, and...

256
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:44,519
no, she will paint a room
a really bright color

257
00:10:44,561 --> 00:10:47,564
without even checking with you.

258
00:10:47,606 --> 00:10:50,775
Okay...?

259
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:54,070
And she uses sex as a weapon.

